=== 2026-09-06, re-run so the output can name the lens it was measured against ===
Re-run of dictionary_geometry.py against the same committed output/states.npz and
the same pinned lens file. Nothing else changed and no decomposition was run. The
fifth review of pull request 84 found that this diagnostic opened the lens with no
gate and overwrote output/dictionary_geometry.json with nothing in it to say which
lens file had produced the numbers, although this record's explanation of the
dictionary's anisotropy, meaning the packing of the 50,257 lens directions around
one common direction, rests on that file. The script now calls the same
pinned-lens gate as the decomposition and the readout (lens_gate.py): the file
must match the digest and byte count specification section 3 pins, and it must
match the digest output/shares.json records for the decomposition. The committed
shares file predates that digest field, so the second check reports that it cannot
be applied rather than passing silently. Effect on the output: every number is
unchanged, a leaf-by-leaf comparison of the old and new files found all 252 values
in the twelve per-layer blocks identical, 0 changed and 0 removed, and the note
field identical; the only difference is the new metadata block naming the lens
file, its size of 12,980,477 bytes, its SHA-256 digest, which is
d1800a1335ada089ef2e1ec0e4bd4d5bd61e6011eacc31f8618fdb3d10aae762, and the absence
of a recorded decomposition digest. Wall clock 38 seconds, of which about 28 seconds is loading
the unembedding matrix and the lens.
